  {
   "id": "09_C10_part1-025",
   "finding": "consistency flag (t^2 label)",
   "old": "§C10.3b's Gaussian mode-shape and truncation factor ($t^2=0.915^2\\approx0.84$, where $t$ is the fraction of a Gaussian beam's power passed by the finite aperture) would lower the results below by a further ≈16%.",
   "new": "§C10.3b's truncation factor ($t^2=0.915^2\\approx0.84$, where $t$ is the fraction of a Gaussian beam's power that the finite aperture passes one way, counted once on transmit and once on receive) would lower the results below by a further ≈16%.",
