   "finding": "report #5 (residual)",
   "old": "hence $60\\times9.0=540$ W to $60\\times26.4\\approx1{,}590$ W. Si trunks (the input waveguides that carry the full power before it is split among elements) are limited by two-photon absorption, a nonlinear loss that grows with intensity (§C8.2); SiN handles watts;",
